I reckon those people who say 3.1 is easier are using save/restore.
I don't know how many good games have been lost to being put to sleep or
paralysed or whatever by monsters. There's not a lot you can do about
it.
Quite recently, I got polymorphed by a trap into a black dragon. Next
level down was the mall. I thought, let's have some fun. So I ate all
the watchmen, and then started on the shopkeepers. The first guy was
carrying a wand of make invisible, but that wasn't a huge problem. But
the next shopkeeper had a wand of sleep, and zapped me first thing.
Game over! Shit! Do these guys always have a wand on them now?

Floating eyes seem more mobile now too. Is this just my imagination?
They seem to deliberately move so you run into them. Little bastards!

>    yeah, its good to see more shops with lot more stuff in them. Kinda
>like K-Mart now. But I found one thing wrong with 3.1 now with pets 
>stealing from stores. They steal everything from the store except for
>armor stuff. Grrrr! They'll take everything except the ever so useful
>armor. This has happened around 10 times with me already. Has this ever
>happen to anyone else?

They only seem to avoid stealing suits of armour. They are probably a
little big for them to carry. They still pick up cloaks, boots, gloves,
etc. BTW, what about big pets? Or even pet humanoids? What does your pet
Uruk-hai do in an armour shop?

If you haven't enough money for a suit of armour, sell the most
expensive stuff you have back to the shopkeeper, and get your pet to
re-steal it. Then buy your armour. You may have to be content with
splint mail or similar until you can afford that +2 dwarvish mithril. 

